  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1210 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nHigh pressure and summer-time heat continue in the extended as we\nwrap up July. H500 high pressure remains strong overhead, but\nmodels show hints of the high pressure center shifting westward\naway from the High Plains towards the first week of August. In the\nmeantime, hot triple digit heat will continue through the week.\nMonday and Tuesday could potentially be the hottest days of the\nweek, with NBM highs reaching 110 in some isolated locations. PoPs\nwill also remain low during the week due to the position of the\nhigh pressure center and our modest moisture profiles. Areas most\nlikely to receive precipitation, if any, will be our northwest\nzones where convection off the high terrain may have the \nappropriate steering flow to move into that area.\n\nRangel",
